{
  "description": "Lane payloads: the plaintext of an application message. Old devices send a bare block array; the operator's agent sends an object with origin and blocks; a current device sends an object with blocks, its own ref and, on a reply, reply_to. Each `decodes_to` is what a client must read; `decodes_to: null` means the plaintext must be refused as not a chat payload. Unknown keys are ignored, at the top level and inside reply_to. A malformed ref or reply_to never refuses the payload: it decodes as absent. Keys absent from `decodes_to` (ref, reply_to, and reply_to's ref and by_session) are absent from the decoded value, never null.",
